ecause you think that you may  get targeted i've been targeted  all my service i actually honestly  didn't give a damn because what meant  more to me was standing up to be counted  and making sure that that kind of  behavior is eradicated  is the uk police um  are police forces around the uk  institutionally misogynistic do you  think  well i think that um the review for the  met police review and take undertaken by  um  sorry  um  i forgot her name casey i've on my  apologies but um i do think yes that  there's some form of misogyny that is  becoming far far more prevalent than  perhaps what even policing has probably  recognized and i think that needs to be  dealt with very very quickly  well let's talk about that then i mean  going forward what needs to be done  because it there needs to be a huge  cultural shift doesn't that  well i think some forces have already  recognized across the uk that there are  some serious changes that need to be  made i know that martin hewitt from the  national police chief council and  working with the with the npcc has  already indicated that there needs to be  some serious changes the metropolitan  police have uh you know um instigated  their own in like review with um as i  just mentioned but the fact is that i  think in some forces and i think my  metropolitan police i've been very clear  as much as i have huge respect for the  commissioner i think that it's time for  some new leadership and some new  direction  so you think crested dick needs to go  i think it needs new direction and i  think that probably answers the question  that you're asking yes yeah okay all  right we appreciate your time short  notice as well former detective  superintendent for the met  shabnam choudhury thank you
 

